 "findings": [
  "The southbound queue at a red light stands still for a minute or more. stopped_vehicle ignores anything queued behind the stop line while the signal is red, and congestion only counts when the queue is still stuck on green.",
  "Buses wait at the northbound stop for 20 to 60 s. We cut the bus stop out of the stopped_vehicle zone instead of raising the time threshold for everyone.",
  "Cyclists and delivery riders come out of the detector as a person plus a bicycle or motorcycle. We pair them by box overlap and speed so they are treated as vehicles, not jaywalkers.",
  "The afternoon clips are framed about 20 px differently from the morning ones. Every clip is registered to one reference view before any zone test, so a stop line drawn once works everywhere.",
  "Two signal heads face the camera and stay readable at dusk. Reading the lamp colour gave us red_light and stop_line without any learned model.",
  "Near the north crossing one metre is 25 to 30 px of the reference view, so a walking pedestrian moves about 4 px between our 10 fps samples. Rule thresholds are in reference pixels and mean the same thing in every clip only because every clip is registered first."
 ]
}